{"id":29567,"slug":"to-sleep-with-anger","title":"To Sleep with Anger","year":1990,"country":"United States","duration":102,"spine":963,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29567-to-sleep-with-anger","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/a9eddcb66dd21abdced90ddc76aeca6c/46yurEoaBasJdHdF47DqXpPZtCQZPf_large.jpg","description":"\nA slow-burning masterwork of the early 1990s, this third feature by Charles Burnett is a singular piece of American mythmaking. In a towering performance, Danny Glover plays the enigmatic southern drifter Harry, a devilish charmer who turns up out of the blue on the South Central Los Angeles doorstep of his old friends. In short order, Harry’s presence seems to cast a chaotic spell on what appeared to be a peaceful household, exposing smoldering tensions between parents and children, tradition and change, virtue and temptation. Interweaving evocative strains of gospel and blues with rich, poetic-realist images, To Sleep with Anger is a sublimely stirring film from an autonomous artistic sensibility, a portrait of family resilience steeped in the traditions of African American mysticism and folklore.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Charles Burnett","slug":"charles-burnett"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Danny Glover","role":"Harry","slug":"danny-glover"},{"actor":"Paul Butler","role":"Gideon","slug":"paul-butler"},{"actor":"Mary Alice","role":"Suzie","slug":"mary-alice"},{"actor":"Carl Lumbly","role":"Junior","slug":"carl-lumbly"},{"actor":"Vonetta McGee","role":"Pat","slug":"vonetta-mcgee"},{"actor":"Richard Brooks","role":"Babe Brother","slug":"richard-brooks"},{"actor":"Ralph Sheryl Lee","role":"Linda","slug":"ralph-sheryl-lee"},{"actor":"Ethel Ayler","role":"Hattie","slug":"ethel-ayler"},{"actor":"Julius Harris","role":"Herman","slug":"julius-harris"},{"actor":"Sy Richardson","role":"Marsh","slug":"sy-richardson"},{"actor":"Davis Roberts","role":"Okra Tate","slug":"davis-roberts"},{"actor":"DeForest Covan","role